{
  "version": "1.0",
  "req_id": "REQ-003",
  "verdict": "needs_more_hardening",
  "summary": "The candidate is materially improved and now covers the visible REQ-003 API surface: POST /documents, GET /documents/{documentId}, explicit reject paths, storage rollback on storage failure, upload audit before processing dispatch, and meaningful acceptance-style tests. However, it is still not promotion-ready. The slice violates the declared shared/common reuse contract by defining storage, event, and audit adapter protocols inside the intake module and by staging shared auth/contracts as part of the REQ-003 payload. It also leaves an operational integrity gap: if processing dispatch fails, the request returns 500 but the uploaded document and audit remain persisted with no durable retry/outbox guarantee, so the intake command does not reliably complete its 'persist and emit work' outcome under failure. CI evidence is also below backend lane expectations.",
