  },
  "shared_common_assessment": {
    "score": 1,
    "max": 5,
    "assessment": "This is the strongest negative area. REQ-003 was supposed to reuse shared storage, audit, events, and authz seams. Instead, storage, audit, and event ports are defined inside backend.documents.intake.contracts, and shared auth/contracts are staged as part of the REQ output. That creates ownership ambiguity and promotion collision risk rather than clean shared/common reuse."
